---
// A real Astro route rather than public/admin/index.html.
//
// Files in public/ are served by exact path only, since `astro dev` does no
// directory-index resolution, so /admin/ 404s in development even though
// Netlify serves it fine in production. As a page it works in both.
//
// config.yml stays in public/ so the CMS fetches it unprocessed.
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>Content Manager</title>
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex" />
</head>
<body>
  <!--
    Sveltia CMS, a drop-in replacement for Decap that reads the same config.yml.
    No Netlify Identity widget: Sveltia has no git-gateway backend, so
    config.yml authenticates against GitHub directly.
    is:inline keeps Astro from trying to bundle the CDN module.
  -->
  <script is:inline type="module" src="https://unpkg.com/@sveltia/cms/dist/sveltia-cms.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
